"""Lecture 27 vignette pool C -- Arterial Occlusive Disease and Aortic Aneurysm:
abdominal and thoracic aortic aneurysm, pseudoaneurysm and aortic dissection.

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.

Patient vignettes with a varied lead-in. Aneurysm diameters in stems never sit
on a threshold (4.5, 5.0, 5.5 or 6.0 cm), abdominal growth is judged per six
months and thoracic growth per year, and slide 119's filing of dissection under
true aneurysms is not used. Scope caps live in cms_e5l27_scope.py.
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
